.TH EUCLID-CLI-ETS-CREATE-SERVER 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ets-create-server \- define a new FTP or SFTP transfer server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ets create-server
.BR \-\-server\-id | \-n
.I NAME
.BR \-\-port | \-p
.I PORT
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I BUCKET
[\fB\-\-protocol\fR|\fB\-P\fR \fIPROTOCOL\fR]
[\fB\-\-address\fR|\fB\-a\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-\-users\fR|\fB\-u\fR \fILIST\fR]
[\fB\-\-groups\fR|\fB\-g\fR \fILIST\fR]
[\fB\-\-host\-key\fR|\fB\-k\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-pasv\-min\fR \fIPORT\fR]
[\fB\-\-pasv\-max\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Defines a new FTP or SFTP transfer server fronting an ESM bucket.
Clients authenticate with their EAM credentials and are admitted if they
are named by
.B \-\-users
or belong to one of
.BR \-\-groups ;
whatever they upload is stored as an object in the bucket, which is what
every listing and download then reads back.
.PP
The server is created
.IR stopped .
Nothing listens on
.I PORT
until
.BR euclid-cli-ets-start-server (1)
marks it as one that should run.
.PP
The bucket is resolved when the server is created, not when it starts,
so a misspelled bucket name is reported here rather than surfacing later
as a server that runs but stores nothing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-server\-id " " \fINAME\fR
Name identifying the server, unique across the installation. Also the
name the manager runs its process under, which is why a duplicate is
rejected. Required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
TCP port to listen on. Rejected if another transfer server already uses
it, since the second one to start would otherwise fail to bind with
nothing in its definition explaining why. Required.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIBUCKET\fR
Name of the ESM bucket this server's clients read and write. Must
already exist. Required.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-protocol " " \fIPROTOCOL\fR
Transfer protocol, \fIFTP\fR or \fISFTP\fR. Defaults to \fISFTP\fR.
Cannot be changed later - delete the server and create it again instead.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-address " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Address to bind to. Defaults to \fI0.0.0.0\fR.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-users " " \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated EAM user IDs allowed to log in, e.g.
\fIalice,bob\fR.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-groups " " \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated EAM user groups whose members may log in. Union with
\fB\-\-users\fR, not intersection: a user may be listed directly, belong
to a permitted group, or both.
.IP
At least one of \fB\-\-users\fR or \fB\-\-groups\fR must be given -
a server naming neither could not be logged in to at all.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-host\-key " " \fIPATH\fR
SFTP only. Private SSH host key file identifying the server to clients.
Generated as an ed25519 key on first start if the file does not exist;
an existing file is never overwritten, since changing a server's
identity makes every client that pinned it refuse to connect. Ignored
for FTP.
.TP
.B \-\-pasv\-min " " \fIPORT\fR
FTP only. Lowest passive data port. Defaults to \fI6000\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-pasv\-max " " \fIPORT\fR
FTP only. Highest passive data port. Defaults to \fI6100\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The server was defined; its full definition is printed as JSON, with
\fIdesiredState\fR \fISTOPPED\fR.
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, neither \fB\-\-users\fR nor
\fB\-\-groups\fR given, the caller is not an authenticated
administrator, the server could not be reached, or the request was
rejected - a duplicate server ID or port (HTTP 409), an unknown bucket
(HTTP 404), or a protocol that is neither FTP nor SFTP (HTTP 400).
.SH EXAMPLES
An SFTP server open to one user group:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets create-server \e
    --server-id sftp1 --protocol SFTP --port 2222 \e
    --bucket dropbox --groups transfer-users
.fi
.RE
.PP
An FTP server on a fixed address with a narrow passive range, open to
two named users:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets create-server \e
    --server-id ftp1 --protocol FTP --port 2121 \e
    --address 10.0.0.5 --bucket dropbox \e
    --users alice,bob --pasv-min 6000 --pasv-max 6020
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-update-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-start-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-delete-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-create-bucket (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-user-group (1)
